# Projectiles leaving the gun, first person (real TF2; ours: launch.scene):
# from 2fort's bridge (0 -300 0) looking 10 degrees down along it, one shot
# each of the Rocket Launcher, the Grenade Launcher and the Stickybomb
# Launcher (tapped), the view model drawn (the Syringe Gun's needles:
# needles.tf2, a puppet Medic's, as this account's Medic has no stock gun),
# recorded every frame at 60 a second for 0.5 s (`<gun>_NN`): where the
# flyer first shows, its trail's start and length, the launch effect's
# direction. Bridge floor at z 0.
#   tools/tf2ref/tf2ref.py scene tools/tf2ref/scenes/launch.tf2 --out <dir>
mp_disable_respawn_times 1
cl_drawhud 0
r_drawvgui 0
r_drawviewmodel 1
fov_desired 90
viewmodel_fov 54
fps_max 60
mat_colorcorrection 0
tf_weapon_criticals 0
host_framerate 0
bot_kick all
sleep 1
jointeam red
sleep 1
joinclass soldier
kill
sleep 7
use tf_weapon_rocketlauncher
sleep 2
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 10 90 0
sleep 3
shot rocket_idle
host_framerate 0.016667
movie rocket
wait 2
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 60
endmovie
host_framerate 0
sleep 2
joinclass demoman
kill
sleep 7
use tf_weapon_grenadelauncher
sleep 2
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 10 90 0
sleep 3
shot pipe_idle
host_framerate 0.016667
movie pipe
wait 2
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 60
endmovie
host_framerate 0
sleep 2
joinclass demoman
kill
sleep 7
use tf_weapon_pipebomblauncher
sleep 2
setpos 0 -300 0
setang 10 90 0
sleep 3
shot sticky_idle
host_framerate 0.016667
movie sticky
wait 2
+attack
wait 2
-attack
wait 60
endmovie
host_framerate 0
sleep 2
